WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.205
Log enough to diagnose the path without
copying unnecessary sensitive text.

00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:11.206
The lab records event type, ticket identifier,
suggestion identifier, queue, and timestamp.

00:00:11.276 --> 00:00:14.668
A suggestion and a reviewed
decision have different meanings.

00:00:14.738 --> 00:00:18.066
Keep correlation identifiers
so you can connect them.

00:00:18.136 --> 00:00:23.661
Prevent duplicate decisions and require the
decision to reference an existing suggestion.

00:00:23.731 --> 00:00:27.529
Metrics should count events honestly
and retain their denominator.

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:31.865
More suggestions do not necessarily
mean more operating value.

00:00:31.935 --> 00:00:35.733
Ten suggestions exist, but
only four decisions were saved.

00:00:35.803 --> 00:00:40.347
Reporting ten successful reviews
hides six incomplete interactions.

00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:45.601
One override may indicate a useful
recovery path rather than a system failure.

00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:50.449
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

00:00:50.519 --> 00:00:56.727
Generate a suggestion, override its queue, save
the decision, then attempt a duplicate save.

00:00:56.797 --> 00:00:58.056
Inspect events.

00:00:58.126 --> 00:01:03.950
The log should contain one suggestion and one
decision with the same suggestion identifier.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:09.844
The override records the chosen queue without
pretending the original suggestion was correct.

00:01:09.914 --> 00:01:14.650
The duplicate request returns a conflict
and does not increase decision count.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.989
Event timestamps show execution, but a separate
measurement design is still needed for the

00:01:20.059 --> 00:01:21.510
Frame Card outcome.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.289
Which event proves a reviewer recorded a choice?

00:01:24.359 --> 00:01:26.301
A. Suggestion created B.

00:01:26.371 --> 00:01:27.821
Decision saved C.

00:01:27.891 --> 00:01:29.257
Health check passed.

00:01:29.327 --> 00:01:30.799
The best answer is B.

00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:34.197
Separate generation, review,
and operating outcomes.
